RF.put("questb:b20",{"8660":{"id":8660,"t":"Doomcaller's Footwraps","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Clay Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Night Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of dominance and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nDoomcaller's Footwraps\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warlock Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8660\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Doomcaller's Footwraps this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Clay Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8500":{"id":8500,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Thorium Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 thorium bars to Dame Twinbraid at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Thorium Bar","desc":"It is so good to see you again ‹name›. I hope that you've been doing well. It's true that we are still in need of thorium bars. If you have them to spare I am collecting them for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"It is so good to see you again, ‹name›. I hope that you've been doing well. It's true that we are still in need of thorium bars. If you have them to spare I am collecting them for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort.","done":"Excellent, ‹class›! A job well done. I'll see to it that those bars get onto the pallet and into the hands of the blacksmiths and engineers that are hard at work building up the supplies for our army. Thank you again, and if you come across more thorium bars be sure to drop by.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":32.1,"n":"Dame Twinbraid","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8580":{"id":8580,"t":"The Horde Needs Firebloom!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 57.","obj":"Bring 20 Firebloom to Batrider Pele'keiki at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Firebloom Firebloom , Sha'ni Proudtusk 18.2 % , Alexia Ironknife 12.5 % , Treant Spirit 3.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Hey, ‹class›. Ya you, mon! There be a whole mess of firebloom the Horde thinkin' they need for this Ahn'Qiraj war effort. Maybe they put it in nice things that go boom? Maybe they give it to the Alliance as fuel for their steam tanks? Who knows? Not Pele'keiki!\nPele'keiki know this though... he know you gonna help him out and bring back lots of the firebloom, right, mon?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Are you done collecting those samples? We could lose Noggle any minute now!","done":"Cross your fingers, friend! Here's to hoping we can save Noggle!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":33.4,"y":69.3,"n":"Batrider Pele'keiki","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"500":{"id":500,"t":"Crushridge Bounty","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 9 Dirty Knucklebones from Crushridge ogres in the Alterac Mountains. Bring them to Marshal Redpath in Southshore.\n9 Dirty Knucklebones Crushridge Plunderer 50 % , Crushridge Warmonger 50 % , Crushridge Enforcer 50 % , Crushridge Mage 50 % and 3 more","desc":"Crushridge ogres have dug an ogre mound up in the Alterac Mountains near the ruined city of Alterac. And my scouts tell me they've taken over those ruins as well.\nWe can't let them get cozy up there; if they think they're safe where they are, then their next step will be to move down into the foothills, which will put them right at our front door!\nGo north to the Alterac Mountains and hunt ogres. Bring me the Dirty Knucklebones they carry and you will earn a nice bounty.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,500\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, are you still hunting ogres? Do you have the knucklebones I had you gather?","done":"Very good, ‹name› You must have hacked through a whole mess of ogres to get all these knucklebones.\nThat should keep them out of our hair. At least, for a while.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":49.5,"y":58.7,"n":"Marshal Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8260":{"id":8260,"t":"Arathor Basic Care Package","lv":34,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nArathor Basic Care Package\nExperience: 270\n+10 reputation with The League of Arathor","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Arathi Basin.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Basin, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Honored with us, and bandages when you are Revered.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46,"y":45.2,"n":"Samuel Hawke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"97940":{"id":97940,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Alanna Raveneye in the Oracle Glade in Teldrassil to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":36.8,"y":34.2,"n":"Alanna Raveneye","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94260":{"id":94260,"t":"Craftsmans writ catseye draught","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Catseye Draught\nCatseye Draught","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Catseye Draught, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nSilithus Darnassus\nSilithus Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Craftsman's Writ: Catseye Draught Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94260","cats":["crafting"]},"94340":{"id":94340,"t":"Craftsmans writ truesilver transformer","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Truesilver Transformer\nTruesilver Transformer","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Truesilver Transformer, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Truesilver Transformer Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94340","cats":["crafting"]},"7940":{"id":7940,"t":"1200 Tickets - Orb of the Darkmoon","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nOrb of the Darkmoon","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (1200)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4740":{"id":4740,"t":"WANTED: Murkdeep!","lv":18,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and slay the murloc known as Murkdeep. The creature is thought to be defending the murloc huts south of Auberdine along the water.\nReport the death of Murkdeep to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\nMurkdeep slain","desc":"Attention!\nA reward is being offered for the death of the murloc \"Murkdeep\". This foul beast is known to be responsible for the death of at least one Sentinel, and is suspected of causing the sinking of at least two cargo vessels in the waters off Darkshore!\nMurkdeep was last spotted at a hutted murloc camp south of Auberdine, and is thought to be protecting the huts there. Reward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\nThe Auberdine Village Council","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTimberland Armguards Ridgeback Bracers Breakwater Girdle\nExperience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings ‹class› - what may the Sentinels assist you with today? Perhaps you are here to inquire about the bounty on Murkdeep?","done":"Well, looks like you're here to more than just inquire! The citizens will be delighted to know that tonight they will sleep a little bit more soundly and safer.\nYou've acted as the executioner of justice for the people of Auberdine today, ‹name›. For that, I would like to offer you this as a suitable reward... for a true hero of the Auberdine people.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.2,"y":44.2,"n":"WANTED: Murkdeep!","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":43.4,"n":"Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1140":{"id":1140,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":28,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free the trapped Highborne souls in Night Run and Satyrnaar, then return to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.\nFree the Highborne soul in Night Run\nFree the Highborne soul in Satyrnaar","desc":"The writing of the orcs is little better than the scribblings of a child. Many of my order scoffed when I chose to learn their tongue, but I have found it beneficial to gain further understanding of my enemies.\nFrom Ilkrud's scribblings, it appears that Athrikus still possesses two soulgems, and they are being held in Night Run and Satyrnaar, satyr-held areas in northeast Ashenvale.\nBe careful out there, ‹name›, the satyrs' blood-soaked temples can be unsettling even for a seasoned ‹class› such as yourself.","rew":"Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I heard whisper once that the satyrs' history is somehow related to that of the night elves, but I have found my esteemed hosts reticent to speak of the matter.","done":"Perhaps the satyrs have been allowed to persist in the forest for too long. I will speak with Elissa about it when next I travel to Auberdine.\nNonetheless, with the soulgems destroyed, Athrikus' power will be greatly diminished. We must seize on this opportunity to eliminate him and his cult.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1380":{"id":1380,"t":"Khan Hratha","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring the Maraudine Key Fragment to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\nMaraudine Key Fragment Khan Hratha\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"‹name›, you helped us against the Magram. Now, help us beat the Maraudine! Kill the head of their clan, Khan Hratha!\nTo face him, blow the Maraudine War Horn. It is atop a high bluff in the Valley of Spears.\nBut to blow the horn, you must gain a warhorn mouthpiece. These are rare, carried only by trusted Maraudine centaur.\nAfter the horn is blown, centaur will come. Kill them until Hratha appears.\nKhan Hratha holds the piece of... a key. Bring it to me...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKolkar Marauder Chain Traitor's Finger\nExperience: 4,300","back":"Is Khan Hratha dead? Do you have the key fragment?","done":"He is dead! Khan Hratha is dead! And now the Maraudine will fall! When the Gelkis rule this land, ‹name›, we will remember you. And the spirits of the earth will sing your name for all time.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"98340":{"id":98340,"t":"The great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.","done":"And so it continues, Father Cenarius.\n<Dendrite makes a quick, invisible gesture in the air above him. A slight aura of power falls over him.>\nGreetings again, Qiy. It is time for you to learn the next perspective of nature: the cat. I will put you on the path to understanding this aspect of druidic life, but much like the bear, it is you that must embrace this learning and propagate it.\nThunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.4,"y":27.6,"n":"Turak Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"420":{"id":420,"t":"Senir's Observations","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Grelin's report to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.\nGrelin's Report\nProvided: Grelin's Report","desc":"The troggs in the tunnel are extremely hostile, and haven't shown any hesitation in attacking travelers through the tunnel. You seem tough enough, though, so you should probably be safe.\nDirections? If you're going to speak with Senir, you'll find him in Kharanos.\nMake your way through the tunnel, and after you come out on the other side, just keep following the road, it'll run right into Kharanos.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"How are you? Like to share a drink with me, perhaps? Not much else to do in the cold.","done":"What's this? Ah, my brother's report. Hmm...\nI told him to be sparing with the use of the King's name, but he didn't listen. No harm, I suppose, though it's sure to ruffle some feathers in the Senate. Not that those weren't some feathers that needed ruffling! Hah!\nNonetheless, I guess that means that I should send my report on to Ironforge as well, but I must admit I'm a bit behind. Bloody cold.\nI should have some work for you later, if you're interested.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":33.5,"y":71.8,"n":"Mountaineer Thalos","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.7,"y":53.8,"n":"Senir Whitebeard","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"1220":{"id":1220,"t":"Captain Vimes","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Spy's Report to Captain Garran Vimes.\nSpy's Report\nProvided: Spy's Report","desc":"Captain Vimes should see the orc report you found, ‹name›. He knows the orcish language better than most. And he should know that there are Horde spies near Theramore!\nThe captain is in the barracks, on the northeastern side of Theramore Isle.","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have something for me?","done":"A report from an orc spy! How did you find this? No matter -- let's see what it says...","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":65.1,"y":47.2,"n":"Theramore Lieutenant","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"2980":{"id":2980,"t":"The Ogres of Feralas","lv":44,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rok Orhan in Camp Mojache wants you to kill 10 Gordunni Shaman, 10 Gordunni Warlocks, and 5 Gordunni Maulers.\nGordunni Shaman slain : 0/ 10\nGordunni Warlock slain : 0/ 10\nGordunni Mauler slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Now that you have proven that you are a true fighter, I trust that you possess the courage to continue with the task at hand.\nTravel to the High Wilderness, southwest of here. There lie some abandoned and destroyed structures, on land that once belonged to the night elves. Look for these ruins, and when you see the withered trees and desecrated terrain, you will find the Gordunni. Push them back.\nThese ogres are much stronger than the ones you faced previously, ‹name›. Be aware.","rew":"Money: 1 25 1 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you found the ruins, ‹name›?","done":"You have proven yourself to be a trustworthy and dependable ally, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Rok Orhan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"660":{"id":660,"t":"Hints of a New Plague?","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Kinelory until she returns to Quae.","desc":"All right, ‹name›. I'm ready if you are.\nShall we?","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The time for talk is done. Protect Kinelory if you care about the people of Hillsbrad at all.","done":"You've done a great service for us, ‹name›. Thank you.\nI hope Kin wasn't too much of a handful down there. She's very friendly, but can be just as deadly when you're her enemy.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.9,"n":"Kinelory","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.8,"n":"Quae","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"9300":{"id":9300,"t":"Page from the Front","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 45 instead of 55.","obj":"Take the Ragged Page to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Ragged Page\nProvided: A Ragged Page","desc":"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","back":"Yes? What do you have there?","done":"How tragic. These words, clearly meant for someone the soldier loved, never made it to their destination. The events detailed happened years ago; I'm not sure if the intended recipient still lives.\nThere is hope yet, however. With the names and information he gives, I might be able to locate the family! It will take some research, but the librarian in Stormwind owes me a favor...\nThank you for bringing this to me. With your help, we may be able to grant someone peace of mind at least.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"2500":{"id":2500,"t":"Badlands Reagent Run","lv":39,"min":36,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire the reagents Ghak Healtouch needs from the Badlands, then return to him in Thelsamar.\n5 Buzzard Gizzard Giant Buzzard 20 % , Starving Buzzard 15 % , Buzzard 5 %\n10 Crag Coyote Fang Feral Crag Coyote 80 % , Rabid Crag Coyote 80 % , Elder Crag Coyote 80 % , Crag Coyote 80 %\n5 Rock Elemental Shard Lesser Rock Elemental 20 % , Greater Rock Elemental 20 % , Enraged Rock Elemental 20 % , Rock Elemental 15 % and 4 more","desc":"‹class›, I would make use of your services. I am an alchemist of some note, and I seek your aid in acquiring some reagents found out in the Badlands.\nI need the following items to replenish my stocks: five buzzard gizzards, ten crag coyote fangs, and five rock elemental shards. Obviously, you can get them off of the beasties themselves; if you're not the fighting type, then find friends who are.\nAcquire these items for me, you'll get some coin out of the deal.\nWell, what say ye?","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you gotten the things I need yet? You won't get paid unless you bring me those reagents.","done":"Ah, well done ‹name›. These should last me for a little while at least. Here is your pay, as promised.\nIf you're interested, I have some more reagents I could use. These, however, are only found in the depths of the Uldaman excavation. They will not be easy to get, but I will make it worth your while if you are interested in helping me again.\nPerhaps something more than some shiny coins, yes?\nLoch Modan Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.1,"y":49.4,"n":"Ghak Healtouch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"1860":{"id":1860,"t":"Speak with Jennea","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.","desc":"We mages have a task that needs doing. One that is vital to the safety of Stormwind and Elwynn forest.\nJennea Cannon has the details. She studies in the wizard's sanctum, in the mage district of Stormwind. You should make your way to her with haste.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"You have been sent to aid me in my task, ‹name›? Good. It is heartening to see young mages eager to help in our cause...\nWhat cause, you ask? In time, young one. You shall know... in time.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.2,"y":66.2,"n":"Zaldimar Wefhellt","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1940":{"id":1940,"t":"Pristine Spider Silk","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Pristine Spider Silk to Wynne Larson in Stormwind.\n8 Pristine Spider Silk Carrion Recluse 80 % , Black Widow Hatchling 80 %","desc":"Your service has been unwavering, ‹name›. I think, perhaps, it is time you had a finer garment, one more suiting your station as an adept mage. If you gather the needed materials, then we will arrange the robe made.\nYou must enter Duskwood and hunt carrion recluse spiders. Extract their silk, but only the finest, most pristine silk will do. When you have enough, take it to Wynne Larson, here in the mage district at the Larson Clothiers. She will craft your robe.","rew":"Experience: 1,600","back":"Ah, yes. The mages of the Wizard's Sanctum said you'd speak with me. Do you have the required silk?","done":"Nice specimens, these. I'll get right to work!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.7,"y":87.6,"n":"High Sorcerer Andromath","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":83.5,"n":"Wynne Larson","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"96260":{"id":96260,"t":"Stronger than steel","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 3 strands of Crystalline Silk from Gloomrise Spinners.\n3 Crystalline Silk","desc":"Have you heard what befell the burial ground at Gloomrise? Giant spiders--rumored to have a venom so strong that it can wake the dead--have spread like wildfire. Nasty business, if you ask me.\nOne of the scouts dispatched to investigate returned half dead and covered in an incredibly resilient, crystalline spider silk. I harvested what I could, but I would highly value more samples of this silk for additional study.\nBring me more of this crystalline silk and I will reward you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSpidersilk Sack Spidersilk Pouch\nYou will also receive:\nCrystal Thread Cloak\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":32.4,"y":20,"n":"Yorn Grimtotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9060":{"id":9060,"t":"Cryptstalker Girdle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Cryptstalker Girdle if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Girdle, 8 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Girdle Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Girdle\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Girdle.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1780":{"id":1780,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"I'll take these to the children this very day. Please be safe, good ‹class›. It is not often men/women of your character show their faces in the city, but you've proven that the paladins here in Stormwind shall never turn their backs on those in need.\nFarewell.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"You've returned so quickly, ‹name›. And what have you accomplished in your time away from the Cathedral?\nHave you helped a noble cause? Perhaps you've learned the value of charity or some more about your obligations to the citizens of Azeroth. Tell me, who have you helped and how... Well, I'm impressed, ‹name›, those are surely the actions of one who follows the Light and values others above oneself.\nSuch sacrifice will always be rewarded in time.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.8,"y":72.2,"n":"Stephanie Turner","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"91860":{"id":91860,"t":"A grim fate","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Investigate Fenris Isle to the east and learn the fate of the Earthen Ring traveling party.","desc":"Out on patrol last night I spotted a group of gnolls dumping a very large body onto a pyre on the shores of Fenris Isle. I didn't see an elf or any smaller corpses, but I'd say this doesn't bode well for them.\nIf you are brave or stupid you are welcome to charge into Fenris Isle to learn more, but if you ask me, its a lot of work to find some snooty elf that's probably long dead.\nI know you paladins love swearing oaths and taking on lost causes, but this one isn't worth it. Trust me.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 440","done":"<The corpse before you was certainly Tauren and you can tell that it was gnawed on heavily before it was tossed onto the pyre. You see no signs of the elf woman that was described to you though. Perhaps she is still alive somewhere deeper in the fortress nearby?\nThis will be dangerous, but there's only one way to find out for sure.>","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":45.6,"y":41.8,"n":"Deathguard Baldren","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65,"y":34.2,"n":"Charred Remains","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"95140":{"id":95140,"t":"Old fire eye","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Moonsilver Blade to destroy Old-Fire Eye in Silverpine Forest.\nOld Fire-Eye slain\nMoonsilver Blade","desc":"I see that you have your weapon now, ‹class›. I pray that it will not fail you.\nThe locals tell me that Old Fire-Eye hunts in a large area south of here and you can generally find him near the gates to Gilneas. Find him, and use your new blade to end him. When it is done, return and you will have the gratitude of the Windshapers.","rew":"You will receive:\nWolfsbane\nExperience: 2,650\n+150 reputation with Undercity\n+150 reputation with Earthen Ring\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Is it done? Is the beast slain?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Banon may now rest in peace.\nIf you would be willing to allow it, I believe that I can impart some magic upon your freshly blooded blade to infuse it with a small measure of the magic of my people.\nIt is done. It's a small thing, and I could scarcely improve such a magnificent blade. Regardless, I will pray to the winds that it serves you well, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.2,"y":41,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94820":{"id":94820,"t":"Contingency plan","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"Your race is so very clever, ‹name›. We are proud to call you allies. And as each day's sun sets, you and your kin grow closer to reclaiming your city, but with the burden of keeping your families safe in exile. That yearning for home must weigh heavily on you.\nWord came from Ironforge just recently. It asked that you return there and speak to High Priestess Mims in the Mystic Ward. I would not keep her waiting. May Elune guide your travels.\nLevel 20 , requires level 20 Difficulty 20 23 27 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94820","cats":["priest"]},"20":{"id":20,"t":"Blackrock Menace","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Battleworn Axes to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.\n10 Battleworn Axe Blackrock Gladiator 50 % , Blackrock Summoner 50 % , Blackrock Hunter 50 % , Blackrock Sentry 50 % and 4 more","desc":"The Blackrock orcs have travelled from the Burning Steppes and claimed Stonewatch Keep to the north. From there they maraud the areas north of Lakeshire and keep its citizens in town, penned like cattle.\nHelp rid Lakeshire of this menace. Kill these Blackrock orcs and bring me ten of their Battleworn Axes as proof.\nAnd although Blackrocks threaten us from the north, we've received reports of more in the southeastern pocket of Redridge. If you find any there, then they too should be hunted.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you been slaying orcs, ‹name›? If so, then show me...","done":"That makes for a lot fewer orcs to worry about, thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":28.4,"y":49,"n":"Marshal Marris","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"180":{"id":180,"t":"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore","lv":26,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore.","obj":"Kill Lieutenant Fangore and return to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire with his paw.\nFangore's Paw Lieutenant Fangore","desc":"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore\nKnown leader of the Shadowhide Gnoll Clan, working under the enemy of the Township and Kingdom, Morganth. By mandate of Magistrate Solomon, this vile betrayer of Stormwind is wanted dead. Show his paw to the Magistrate as proof of his death.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What news do you bring before the Court?","done":"So the evil Lieutenant Fangore is dead? Good riddance to that foul creature. You are very brave, ‹class›. The Township of Lakeshire thanks you for your aid.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.7,"y":46.4,"n":"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8820":{"id":8820,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Ironforge. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":32.8,"n":"Gnomeregan Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":28.6,"n":"Officer Ironbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"2260":{"id":2260,"t":"Erion's Behest","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stormwind City and seek council with Renzik \"The Shiv.\"","desc":"Word of your deeds has spread far and wide, ‹name›. So far, in fact, that Stormwind Intelligence has asked for you by name.\nThe journey is taxing and not without peril, but an opportunity to train under SI:7 should not be taken lightly.\nA new world awaits you, ‹name›. Make your way to Old Town in Stormwind and speak with Renzik \"The Shiv\" at SI:7 headquarters.","rew":"Experience: 575","done":"You have answered SI:7's calling, ‹name› and journeyed from distant shores to join our ranks, however, there is much for you to learn.\nDarnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.5,"y":25.9,"n":"Erion Shadewhisper","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":71.1,"n":"Renzik \"The Shiv\"","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8900":{"id":8900,"t":"Dearest Elenia,","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Slightly Creased Note to Elenia Haydon near the bank in the Undercity.\nSlightly Creased Note\nProvided: Slightly Creased Note","desc":"She was so sad. I could see that, once I saw past her state. I mean, she seemed sad - wouldn't you?\nBut after talking to her, there was a connection. I didn't think anyone could understand what I was thinking, but she could.\nWhen I told the others, they laughed at me, so I never spoke with her again. But I miss her. Can you take this letter to her for me? I want to be sure it finds her hands.","back":"Oh, and to what do I owe this pleasure?","done":"You wouldn't expect an orc to be so eloquent. Of course, we never really had a chance to know them before now. Thank you for bringing this to me.\nOrgrimmar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":51.3,"y":70.2,"n":"Orok Deathbane","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":66.9,"y":45.2,"n":"Elenia Haydon","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8980":{"id":8980,"t":"Zinge's Assessment","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Fenstad Argyle outside the bank in the Undercity.","desc":"This is unexpected. It looks like Fenstad might be on to something after all. I found traces of substances used in mind control potions.\nIt isn't unheard of for perfumes to have some of this, but a few of the ingredients I detected... This is serious alchemy, along the abilities of a member of the Royal Apothecary Society.","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Chocolates Handful of Rose Petals","done":"So, I was right. We must waste no time. We must determine the source of these tainted fragrances.\nHere, to repay you for the purchase of the cologne and perfume.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":66.7,"y":44.7,"n":"Fenstad Argyle","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"100":{"id":100,"t":"Call of Water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 190 experience instead of 1,250, 0.15 times as much.","obj":"Speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water in Silverpine Forest.","desc":"Light explodes as you finish the incantation. The sounds of the water drops hitting the flame have died down and your senses are overcome as the corrupt spirits around you are destroyed.","rew":"Experience: 190","done":"Thanks to you. Thanks to the shamans.\nCorruption ebbs but life continues to wane. Up to shamans to protect life.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":38.3,"y":44.6,"n":"Brazier of Everfount","s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94500":{"id":94500,"t":"Call of water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Fill the Unfilled Blue Waterskin at the waters of Astranaar in Ashenvale and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.\nFull Blue Waterskin","desc":"Take this waterskin and journey deep into the emerald shade o' Ashenvale. Astranaar rests cradled by waters untouched by corruption. Ruins litter the bed o' the lake, hinting at a bygone era. Bring back a sample from the lake. Pure, ancient, and possibly enchanted water.\nIt's the last liquid I need before I send ye back to Norric.\nBoard the boat in Menethil to Auberdine, it stops in Southshore on the way over.\nAnd mind yerself... the forest's got eyes, and they don't blink.","back":"Do you have the water yet, Theinn? If ye haven't made the trek to Kalimdor yet, be careful.","done":"Well done, Theinn! With all three samples in hand, I'll brew ye a vial o' water so pure it'd make the mountains weep. It's the final piece for yer rite o' passage. I'm proud to call ye kin, Theinn. Ye've done ‹class› proud, and I look forward to hearing yer tales in the future.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":65.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Hervdana Saegrund","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8740":{"id":8740,"t":"Twilight Marauders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Twilight Marauder Morna and 5 Twilight Marauders. Report to Windcaller Proudhorn when your task is finished. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.\nTactical Task Briefing IX Rex Ashil\nTwilight Marauder Morna slain\nTwilight Marauder slain : 0/ 5\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing IX","desc":"Bands of mounted Twilight's Hammer cultists have been spotted riding outside the reach of our forces in Cenarion Hold, picking off our smaller patrols and caravans.\nFind and defeat the twilight marauders along with their leader, a terrible warrior by the name of Morna. Report to Windcaller Proudhorn after completing the task.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Followup Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Is your task done yet, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. The twilight marauders were inflicting an unacceptable number of casualties on our patrols. Here's your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"97220":{"id":97220,"t":"Philmors favor","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Gatehouse Shipment to the stockroom entrance located in Trias' Cheese shop in the Trade District\nProvided: Gatehouse Shipment","desc":"Every day this week we've been short dockhands.\nCare to ease the stress on our cargo schedule?\nTake this package to the stockroom entrance of the Gatehouse. You'll find it inside Trias' Cheese shop on the second floor. The mistress, Elaine, will be quite familiar with the deliveries. The Gatehouse often has shipments arriving with more discretion to allow for ceremonial surprises on behalf of the guard's officers.","back":"You looking to fill a crate with our finest aged wheels?","done":"Oh, dear. You think we want to carry that up the stairs ourselves? Keeping the valuables intact is your responsibility up until the point you drop it off.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":30.4,"y":29,"n":"Manifest Clerk Philmor","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":63.4,"n":"Elaine Trias","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"340":{"id":340,"t":"Chapter II","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring pages 10, 11, 14 and 16 of Nesingwary's The Green Hills of Stranglethorn to Barnil Stonepot in order to complete Chapter II.\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 10 Mok'rash 1.9 % , Bookie Herod 1.6 % , Saltscale Tide Lord 1.3 % , Garr Salthoof 1.2 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 11 Verifonix 4.4 % , Gluggle 3.4 % , Negolash 2.4 % , Roloch 1.8 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 14 Negolash 2.4 % , Verifonix 1.8 % , Roloch 1.8 % , Sergeant Malthus 1.6 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 16 Verifonix 6.3 % , Roloch 5.5 % , Negolash 2.9 % , Brutus 1.8 % and 4 more","desc":"Chapter II was chock full of exciting tales of panther and tiger hunting. I could just kick myself for letting the pages blow away!\nIt seems I was able to recover all of the pages with the exception of pages 10, 11, 14, and 16.","rew":"You will receive:\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter II\nExperience: 775","back":"We still need pages 10, 11, 14 and 16 to complete Chapter II, ‹name›.","done":"Chapter II is finally complete! Well done!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.5,"n":"Barnil Stonepot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"580":{"id":580,"t":"Whiskey Slim's Lost Grog","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Whiskey Slim in Booty Bay wants you to bring him the bottles of Pupellyverbos Port he lost.\n12 Pupellyverbos Port Pupellyverbos Port","desc":"We was splicin' the mainbrace somethin' fierce off of the Overlook Cliffs, ol' Hinterlands just in the distance. Thought the seas was goin' to swallow us whole.\nOl' Slim knows all about liquid courage! Cap'n had a crate of Pupellyverbos Port we commandeered from a privateer en route to Stormwind.\nSo when that storm off of Hinterlands hit, I busted into the grog. Big wave hit and tossed them bottles overboard. Cap'n is goin' to give me a taste o' the cat if ye don't help me get 'em back though!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Rumsey Rum\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Sink me! I'm almost outta booze here! Cap'n is goin' to weigh anchor and Ol' Slim will be caught dry as the Tanaris Desert. And once he discovers his port is missing. . . blimey!","done":"Shiver me timbers! Ye found the Cap'n's grog!\nI owe ye big time, friend.\nSeems like a storm is a brewin' outside. Maybe I'll just keep warm with one o' these here bottles while we wait for it to pass....\nStranglethorn Vale The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.4,"n":"Whiskey Slim","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3380":{"id":3380,"t":"The Sunken Temple","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Marvon Rivetseeker in Tanaris.","desc":"There are restless spirits in this world, ‹name›. There are spirits that have been tainted by their isolation, bound to an ancient evil...\nI have heard of a place that lies deep below the surface of the earth -- banished there by powers greater than I have ever seen.\nIf you wish to learn more of this place; the Sunken Temple, seek out a goblin named Marvon Rivetseeker. He has studied many ancient areas of the world, and was last known to have left his home in Ratchet to study the troll ruins in Tanaris.","rew":"Experience: 3,650","done":"Yes, the Sunken Temple, I can say that I have seen it with my own eyes. Perhaps you'd like to hear more about it?\nYou look like the adventurous type -- I know things that may intrigue you...\nFeralas Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.7,"y":45.9,"n":"Marvon Rivetseeker","e":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"900":{"id":900,"t":"Samophlange","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Close off the Fuel Control Valve, the Regulator Valve and the Main Control Valve then use the control console again.\nShut off Main Control Valve\nShut off Fuel Control Valve\nShut off Regulator Valve","desc":"The three control valves are currently opened. The various readings on the control panel lead you to presume that they must be shut off before the apparatus can be shut off.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Blinking lights on the control console indicate that the main control valves have not been closed off.","done":"The lights indicating the three control valves dim as they are shut off. Green lights slowly fade into yellow, and the switch controlling the apparatus is now moveable, with the valves closed, it can be turned off.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.4,"y":11.6,"n":"Control Console","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1060":{"id":1060,"t":"Letter to Jin'Zil","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Darsok's letter to Jin'Zil within his cave in Malaka'Jin, in Stonetalon.\nLetter to Jin'Zil\nProvided: Letter to Jin'Zil","desc":"You've done so well for me, ‹name›. You're a regular lucky rabbit's foot and there's something I want you to see.\nThe harpies are not from around the Barrens. They come from a place called Stonetalon, far to the northwest of here. Though it is probably a dangerous place for you, I need this letter delivered to an old friend of mine who lives there, a witch doctor by the name of Jin'Zil.\nHe'll be happy to know that Serena Bloodfeather is dead, and I think you'll find Stonetalon an interesting place.","rew":"Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You seem a shady character. You have something for me to see?","done":"Ahh, a letter from Darsok. I have not heard from him in many years.\nSo the last of the Bloodfeathers are dead, eh? That is good news, I can remember when my friend Rokhan went with that crazy mok'nathal to kill her older sister. Ah, to be young again, like you.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.6,"y":30.9,"n":"Darsok Swiftdagger","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":74.5,"y":97.9,"n":"Witch Doctor Jin'Zil","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2340":{"id":2340,"t":"Deliver the Gems","lv":44,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Necklace and Gem Salvage to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.\nNecklace and Gem Salvage\nProvided: Necklace and Gem Salvage","desc":"Any necklace setting and gem will work, so long as they are the same material. This power source, however, is what will bring the magic back to the necklace... I hope.\nI'll gladly supply the gems needed for your version of the necklace, so long as the power source actually works.\nHead to Orgrimmar and keep your end of the bargain with Droffers and Son Salvage. Just keep your mouth shut about our deal, and when you get back I might have a wonderful surprise for you.","rew":"Money: 1 25 1 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Well, look who it is! Took your sweet time getting here, I see. Let's hope this isn't a waste of my time! You'll not get paid unless you have everything I asked for. And trust me on this - we'll be double and triple checking everything!","done":"Yep, it's all here. Say, mind if we keep the bag too? No? Thanks, appreciate it! Har!\nThis necklace will be our greatest haul yet! Don't feel too bad though; I'm sure the necklace wouldn't fit you anyway. Har again!\nA deal is a deal, so here's your fee for the salvage. Our business is done here for now; check back later to see if we have more work. Until then, beat it!\nBadlands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.6,"y":36.5,"n":"Dran Droffers","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"980":{"id":980,"t":"The New Springs","lv":55,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Winterspring and speak with Donova Snowden.","desc":"Now, I've heard about other hot springs in a place called Winterspring, far to the north of here. The strange thing is, there are no volcanoes anywhere near them. Interesting, I know.\nWell, if you want to find out more, you should head to Winterspring and speak to a friend of mine. Her name is Donova Snowden, and she is currently staying by the hot springs there.\nThanks again for helping me with my thermometer! See you later!","rew":"Experience: 2,800","done":"Hi there, ‹name›. Yes, what Krakle told you is true...\nUn'Goro Crater Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":30.9,"y":50.4,"n":"Krakle","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"8420":{"id":8420,"t":"Hot and Itchy","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a piece of felcloth to Impsy in Felwood.\nFelcloth Xorothian Dreadsteed 34.8 % , Felcular 9.9 % , Lord Banehollow 9.9 % , Doomguard Commander 8.6 % and 4 more","desc":"Maybe this sounds strange coming from an imp, but I'd like a pet of my own. I really would. It's just not fair that Niby gets me and I get nothing!\nIn fact, it doesn't even need to be a living pet. I'd need something to start making it with, like some felcloth. The satyrs here in Felwood sometimes have felcloth, so you'd just have to kill enough of them until you find some. That doesn't sound so bad, does it?","rew":"Experience: 3,800","back":"Do you have my felcloth?","done":"Wow! You are too kind. Especially for a warlock!\n<Impsy holds the felcloth to his face.>\nOh how I love the feel of it, the way it burns your skin and weaves evil thoughts through the mind...","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1700":{"id":1700,"t":"Grimand Elmore","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Furen's Notes to Grimand Elmore.\nFuren's Notes\nProvided: Furen's Notes","desc":"I made a copy of my notes on the techniques I learned while making your armor, and I need them sent to Grimand Elmore. He's here in the Dwarven District, in the weapon shop.\nAnd duck when you give these to him. He's fiercely proud of his skills, and won't like the idea of learning something from me...","rew":"Experience: 575","back":"Hello, and well met. How might I be of service to you?","done":"Furen wrote this? How dare he! Why, I taught him everything he knows! To think he could teach me something is outrageous! Outrageous!\nHm... but there is something in his notes that I'd like to try...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5060":{"id":5060,"t":"Locked Away","lv":55,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dalson Cabinet Key Farmer Dalson","rew":"You will receive:\nFarmer Dalson's Shotgun Dalson Family Wedding Ring\nMoney: 2 50 2 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,050","back":"An extremely sturdy cabinet stands before you, securely fastened shut by a built-in lock. The front of the cabinet is deeply scratched and marked. This could be surmised as being from numerous and violent failed attempts to reveal whatever secrets the cabinet currently obfuscates from view.\nIf you are going to open this cabinet, you will need to find the key.","done":"The key taken from Farmer Dalson's ghoulish remains fits the lock perfectly. The doors of the cabinet swing open, revealing several items that remain intact and appear quite valuable.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":47.4,"y":49.6,"n":"Locked Cabinet","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5220":{"id":5220,"t":"Return to Chillwind Camp","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Dalson's Tears Bottle\nProvided: Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle","desc":"You carefully fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's ichors for what you consider to be suitably sized sample.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+50 reputation with Stormwind\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"We know that each cauldron employs a different mix of reagents to generate its plague-inducing toxin; likewise, we know that we will need to develop a counter agent that is unique for each cauldron. Your sample from Dalson's Tears will be the key to figure out that cauldron's distinct reagent requirement.","done":"Ah, there is plenty in here for study. Well done, ‹name›!\nFor now, the next step is in our hands. We'll need to produce a list of reagents that, when combined with what is already in the cauldron, will act as its counter.\nThe only way we will be able to introduce this is by placing the reagents into the cauldron directly. Alchemist Arbington will have more information on that, so be sure to speak with him at your earliest convenience.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":46.2,"y":51.9,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]}});